window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-83d4edfaf8cd6445"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"dynamic-groups\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">动态群组</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>动态群组使用身份提供商通过 SCIM 发送的用户属性来组织工作区成员。你可以用受支持的属性（例如部门或位置）定义成员资格规则。随着这些属性变化，群组会更新成员：加入符合规则的人，移除不再符合规则的人。</p> <p>例如，动态群组可以包含部门为 Engineering、位置为 London 的成员。你在 ChatGPT Admin 中管理规则，用户属性则由身份提供商提供。</p> <p><a id=\"before-you-begin\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">开始之前</h2> <ul> <li>以工作区所有者或管理员身份，登录支持动态群组的工作区。</li> <li>为工作区配置 SCIM 预配，并确保身份提供商会发送你要使用的属性。</li> <li>选择与身份提供商实际发送值相符的属性值。请参阅本指南中的受支持属性和载荷路径。</li> </ul> <p>群组成员资格与功能权限相互独立。成员适用的角色、席位类型及产品使用资格，仍然决定其访问权限。访问模型见<a href=\"#/article/a-10dd8667120ae18c\">群组与预配</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"create-a-dynamic-group\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">创建动态群组</h2> <ol> <li>打开 <a href=\"https://admin.openai.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT Admin（需联网）</a>，选择你的工作区。</li> <li>在 <strong>Identity &amp; access（身份与访问）</strong> 下，选择 <strong>Groups &amp; roles（群组与角色）</strong>。</li> <li>使用 <strong>+</strong> 按钮选择 <strong>Create group（创建群组）</strong>。</li> <li>输入群组名称，例如 <strong>Demo</strong>，开启 <strong>Dynamic group（动态群组）</strong>，然后选择 <strong>Next（下一步）</strong>。</li> </ol> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">创建 Demo 群组，并开启 Dynamic group 选项 · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/dynamic-groups/create-dynamic-group.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>创建 Demo 群组，并开启 Dynamic group 选项 · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/dynamic-groups/create-dynamic-group.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开官网原始媒体</a></figcaption> </figure> <ol> <li>在 <strong>Add membership rules（添加成员资格规则）</strong> 下，选择 <strong>Attribute（属性）</strong>、<strong>Operator（运算符）</strong> 和 <strong>Value（值）</strong>。在本例中，选择 <strong>department</strong>、<strong>Equals（等于）</strong>，并输入 <strong>Engineering</strong>。</li> <li>选择 <strong>Add condition（添加条件）</strong>，再添加一条规则。本例选择 <strong>location</strong>、<strong>Equals（等于）</strong>，并输入 <strong>London</strong>。</li> </ol> <p>成员必须满足<strong>所有条件</strong>。下面的示例匹配部门为 Engineering <strong>并且</strong>位置为 London 的成员。</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">成员资格规则要求 department 等于 Engineering，且 location 等于 London · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/dynamic-groups/membership-rules.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>成员资格规则要求 department 等于 Engineering，且 location 等于 London · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/dynamic-groups/membership-rules.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开官网原始媒体</a></figcaption> </figure> <ol> <li>选择 <strong>Create（创建）</strong>。打开群组的 <strong>Settings（设置）</strong> 标签页，检查名称和成员资格规则。</li> </ol> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">Demo 群组的设置，显示已保存的动态成员资格规则及 Re-sync 按钮 · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/dynamic-groups/group-settings.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>Demo 群组的设置，显示已保存的动态成员资格规则及 Re-sync 按钮 · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/dynamic-groups/group-settings.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开官网原始媒体</a></figcaption> </figure> <p>创建群组会保存其成员资格规则。选择 <strong>Re-sync（重新同步）</strong>，才能将这些规则应用到工作区现有成员。</p> <p><a id=\"edit-membership-rules\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">编辑成员资格规则</h2> <p>要更改哪些成员符合动态群组条件：</p> <ol> <li>打开群组，选择 <strong>Settings（设置）</strong>。</li> <li>编辑成员资格规则，选择 <strong>Save changes（保存更改）</strong>。</li> <li>选择 <strong>Re-sync（重新同步）</strong>，将保存的规则应用到工作区现有成员。</li> </ol> <p><strong>Save changes（保存更改）</strong> 只保存规则，不会开始重新同步。<strong>Re-sync（重新同步）</strong> 使用已保存的规则；如果还有未保存的更改，该选项不可用。</p> <p><a id=\"re-sync-membership\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">重新同步成员资格</h2> <p>使用 <strong>Re-sync（重新同步）</strong>，根据群组当前规则以及工作区中已有的 SCIM 属性，重新评估成员资格。</p> <ol> <li>打开动态群组，选择 <strong>Settings（设置）</strong>。</li> <li>在 <strong>Membership rules（成员资格规则）</strong> 中，选择 <strong>Re-sync（重新同步）</strong>。</li> <li>查看 <strong>Syncing group membership（正在同步群组成员资格）</strong> 状态面板。排队中的同步可能会显示 <strong>Starts in（距离开始）</strong> 倒计时，然后才开始处理。你可以收起面板，也可以在 <strong>Cancel sync（取消同步）</strong> 选项仍可用时取消同步。</li> <li>处理完成后，打开 <strong>Group members（群组成员）</strong>，检查结果。</li> </ol> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">正在同步群组成员资格的面板，显示倒计时及 Cancel sync 控件 · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/dynamic-groups/resync-status.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>正在同步群组成员资格的面板，显示倒计时及 Cancel sync 控件 · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/dynamic-groups/resync-status.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开官网原始媒体</a></figcaption> </figure> <p>同步期间，成员资格规则控件不可用。取消同步可能使成员资格只更新了一部分。更改规则后，请先保存，再次运行 <strong>Re-sync（重新同步）</strong>，以应用已保存的规则。如果预期成员没有出现，请检查其 SCIM 属性是否已传入工作区，以及属性值是否满足每一个条件。</p> <p><a id=\"view-a-members-scim-attributes\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"scim\">查看成员的 SCIM 属性</h2> <p>使用成员的个人资料卡片，查看工作区中可用的 SCIM 属性值，并与动态群组的成员资格规则比较。</p> <ol> <li>在 <strong>Identity &amp; access（身份与访问）</strong> 下，选择 <strong>Members（成员）</strong>。</li> <li>按姓名或电子邮件搜索成员，然后选择其姓名，打开个人资料卡片。</li> <li>查看 <strong>SCIM attributes（SCIM 属性）</strong> 表格，其中列出了每个可用属性及其值。</li> </ol> <p>下面的示例显示一位测试成员的 SCIM 属性值，包括 <code>department</code>、<code>title</code> 和 <code>costCenter</code>。</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">成员个人资料卡片：姓名、电子邮件及群组名称已遮盖，显示 SCIM 属性名称和属性值 · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/dynamic-groups/member-scim-attributes.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>成员个人资料卡片：姓名、电子邮件及群组名称已遮盖，显示 SCIM 属性名称和属性值 · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/dynamic-groups/member-scim-attributes.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开官网原始媒体</a></figcaption> </figure> <p><a id=\"supported-scim-attributes\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"scim_1\">受支持的 SCIM 属性</h2> <p>下表列出了受支持的属性名称，以及每个属性能够识别的用户载荷字段。本目录中的所有属性都使用字符串类型，包括 <code>isAdmin</code>。</p> <p>普通字段名表示顶层字段。以 <code>/</code> 开头的路径表示指定 SCIM 扩展对象中的字段。例如，<code>/urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:extension:enterprise:2.0:User/department</code> 表示 <code>urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:extension:enterprise:2.0:User</code> 对象中的 <code>department</code>。</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>属性名称</th> <th>SCIM 载荷中可识别的字段</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>department</code></td> <td><code>department</code><br><code>/urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:extension:enterprise:2.0:User/department</code><br><code>/urn:scim:schemas:extension:enterprise:1.0/department</code><br><code>/urn:scim:schemas:extension:enterprise:2.0/department</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>title</code></td> <td><code>title</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>manager</code></td> <td><code>manager</code><br><code>/urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:extension:enterprise:2.0:User/manager/value</code><br><code>/urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:extension:enterprise:2.0:User/manager/displayName</code><br><code>/urn:scim:schemas:extension:enterprise:1.0/manager/value</code><br><code>/urn:scim:schemas:extension:enterprise:1.0/manager/displayName</code><br><code>/urn:scim:schemas:extension:enterprise:2.0/manager/value</code><br><code>/urn:scim:schemas:extension:enterprise:2.0/manager/displayName</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>costCenter</code></td> <td><code>costCenter</code><br><code>/urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:extension:enterprise:2.0:User/costCenter</code><br><code>/urn:scim:schemas:extension:enterprise:1.0/costCenter</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>division</code></td> <td><code>division</code><br><code>/urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:extension:enterprise:2.0:User/division</code><br><code>/urn:scim:schemas:extension:enterprise:1.0/division</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>organization</code></td> <td><code>organization</code><br><code>/urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:extension:enterprise:2.0:User/organization</code><br><code>/urn:scim:schemas:extension:enterprise:1.0/organization</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>userType</code></td> <td><code>userType</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>country</code></td> <td><code>country</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>isAdmin</code></td> <td><code>isAdmin</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>location</code></td> <td><code>location</code></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>对于 <code>manager</code>，本目录能够识别顶层字段，以及嵌套扩展中的 <code>value</code> 或 <code>displayName</code> 字段。对于 <code>country</code>，请发送表中所示的顶层字段。</p> <p><a id=\"related-documentation\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">相关文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-10dd8667120ae18c\">群组与预配</a></li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"dynamic-groups\">Dynamic groups</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Dynamic groups organize workspace members using user attributes sent by your identity provider through SCIM. You define membership rules using supported attributes, such as department or location. As those attributes change, group membership updates to include people who match the rules and remove people who no longer match.</p> <p>For example, a dynamic group can include members whose department is Engineering and whose location is London. You manage the rules in ChatGPT Admin, while your identity provider supplies the user attributes.</p> <h2 id=\"before-you-begin\">Before you begin</h2> <ul> <li>Sign in as a workspace owner or admin in a workspace where dynamic groups are available.</li> <li>Configure SCIM provisioning for your workspace and make sure your identity provider sends the attributes you want to use.</li> <li>Choose attribute values that match the values your identity provider sends. See the supported attributes and payload paths in this guide.</li> </ul> <p>Group membership and feature permissions are separate. A member’s applicable roles, seat type, and product eligibility still determine access. See <a href=\"#/article/a-10dd8667120ae18c\">Groups and provisioning</a> for the access model.</p> <h2 id=\"create-a-dynamic-group\">Create a dynamic group</h2> <ol> <li>Open <a href=\"https://admin.openai.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT Admin (online)</a> and select your workspace.</li> <li>Under <strong>Identity &amp; access</strong>, select <strong>Groups &amp; roles</strong>.</li> <li>Select <strong>Create group</strong> using the <strong>+</strong> button.</li> <li>Enter a group name, such as <strong>Demo</strong>, turn on <strong>Dynamic group</strong>, and select <strong>Next</strong>.</li> </ol> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">Create the Demo group with Dynamic group enabled · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/dynamic-groups/create-dynamic-group.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>Create the Demo group with Dynamic group enabled · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/dynamic-groups/create-dynamic-group.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <ol> <li>Under <strong>Add membership rules</strong>, choose an <strong>Attribute</strong>, an <strong>Operator</strong>, and a <strong>Value</strong>. In this example, select <strong>department</strong>, <strong>Equals</strong>, and enter <strong>Engineering</strong>.</li> <li>Select <strong>Add condition</strong> to add another rule. For this example, select <strong>location</strong>, <strong>Equals</strong>, and enter <strong>London</strong>.</li> </ol> <p>Members must match <strong>all conditions</strong>. The example below matches members whose department is Engineering <strong>and</strong> whose location is London.</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">Membership rules requiring department to equal Engineering and location to equal London · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/dynamic-groups/membership-rules.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>Membership rules requiring department to equal Engineering and location to equal London · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/dynamic-groups/membership-rules.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <ol> <li>Select <strong>Create</strong>. Open the group’s <strong>Settings</strong> tab to review its name and membership rules.</li> </ol> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">Demo settings with the saved dynamic membership rules and Re-sync button · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/dynamic-groups/group-settings.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>Demo settings with the saved dynamic membership rules and Re-sync button · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/dynamic-groups/group-settings.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <p>Creating the group saves its membership rules. Select <strong>Re-sync</strong> to apply those rules to existing workspace members.</p> <h2 id=\"edit-membership-rules\">Edit membership rules</h2> <p>To change which members qualify for a dynamic group:</p> <ol> <li>Open the group and select <strong>Settings</strong>.</li> <li>Edit its membership rules and select <strong>Save changes</strong>.</li> <li>Select <strong>Re-sync</strong> to apply the saved rules to existing workspace members.</li> </ol> <p><strong>Save changes</strong> stores the rules without starting a re-sync. <strong>Re-sync</strong> uses the saved rules and is unavailable while you have unsaved changes.</p> <h2 id=\"re-sync-membership\">Re-sync membership</h2> <p>Use <strong>Re-sync</strong> to re-evaluate the group’s membership against its current rules and the SCIM attributes already available in the workspace.</p> <ol> <li>Open the dynamic group and select <strong>Settings</strong>.</li> <li>In <strong>Membership rules</strong>, select <strong>Re-sync</strong>.</li> <li>Follow the <strong>Syncing group membership</strong> status panel. A queued sync can show <strong>Starts in</strong> with a countdown before processing begins. You can collapse the panel or use <strong>Cancel sync</strong> while that option is available.</li> <li>After processing finishes, open <strong>Group members</strong> to review the result.</li> </ol> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">The Syncing group membership panel shows a countdown and Cancel sync control · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/dynamic-groups/resync-status.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>The Syncing group membership panel shows a countdown and Cancel sync control · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/dynamic-groups/resync-status.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <p>Membership rule controls are unavailable while the sync is active. Canceling a sync can leave membership partially updated. After making any rule changes, save them and run <strong>Re-sync</strong> again to apply the saved rules. If an expected member is missing, check that their SCIM attributes have reached the workspace and that their values match every condition.</p> <h2 id=\"view-a-members-scim-attributes\">View a member’s SCIM attributes</h2> <p>Use a member’s profile card to check the SCIM attribute values available in your workspace and compare them with your dynamic group’s membership rules.</p> <ol> <li>Under <strong>Identity &amp; access</strong>, select <strong>Members</strong>.</li> <li>Search for the member by name or email, then select their name to open their profile card.</li> <li>Review the <strong>SCIM attributes</strong> table, which lists each available attribute and its value.</li> </ol> <p>The example below shows a test member’s SCIM values, including <code>department</code>, <code>title</code>, and <code>costCenter</code>.</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">Member profile card with name, email, and group names masked, showing SCIM attribute names and values · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/dynamic-groups/member-scim-attributes.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>Member profile card with name, email, and group names masked, showing SCIM attribute names and values · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/dynamic-groups/member-scim-attributes.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <h2 id=\"supported-scim-attributes\">Supported SCIM attributes</h2> <p>The following table lists the supported attribute names and the user-payload fields recognized for each one. All attributes in this catalog use the string type, including <code>isAdmin</code>.</p> <p>A plain field name refers to a top-level field. A path beginning with <code>/</code> identifies a field inside the named SCIM extension object. For example, <code>/urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:extension:enterprise:2.0:User/department</code> refers to <code>department</code> inside the <code>urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:extension:enterprise:2.0:User</code> object.</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Attribute name</th> <th>Recognized fields in the SCIM payload</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>department</code></td> <td><code>department</code><br><code>/urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:extension:enterprise:2.0:User/department</code><br><code>/urn:scim:schemas:extension:enterprise:1.0/department</code><br><code>/urn:scim:schemas:extension:enterprise:2.0/department</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>title</code></td> <td><code>title</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>manager</code></td> <td><code>manager</code><br><code>/urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:extension:enterprise:2.0:User/manager/value</code><br><code>/urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:extension:enterprise:2.0:User/manager/displayName</code><br><code>/urn:scim:schemas:extension:enterprise:1.0/manager/value</code><br><code>/urn:scim:schemas:extension:enterprise:1.0/manager/displayName</code><br><code>/urn:scim:schemas:extension:enterprise:2.0/manager/value</code><br><code>/urn:scim:schemas:extension:enterprise:2.0/manager/displayName</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>costCenter</code></td> <td><code>costCenter</code><br><code>/urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:extension:enterprise:2.0:User/costCenter</code><br><code>/urn:scim:schemas:extension:enterprise:1.0/costCenter</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>division</code></td> <td><code>division</code><br><code>/urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:extension:enterprise:2.0:User/division</code><br><code>/urn:scim:schemas:extension:enterprise:1.0/division</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>organization</code></td> <td><code>organization</code><br><code>/urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:extension:enterprise:2.0:User/organization</code><br><code>/urn:scim:schemas:extension:enterprise:1.0/organization</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>userType</code></td> <td><code>userType</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>country</code></td> <td><code>country</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>isAdmin</code></td> <td><code>isAdmin</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>location</code></td> <td><code>location</code></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>For <code>manager</code>, the catalog recognizes the top-level field and the nested extension <code>value</code> or <code>displayName</code> fields. For <code>country</code>, send the top-level field shown in the table.</p> <h2 id=\"related-documentation\">Related documentation</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-10dd8667120ae18c\">Groups and provisioning</a></li> </ul>"};
